:0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm approving PKT-0110. The diff meets the goal and stays inside scope and budget: 5 files and about 114 changed lines, against limits of 6 files and 800 lines.\n\n**Goal coverage**\n- **Large document:** `gen-inputs.py` generates `large.docx` with 880 paragraphs. `run.cjs` checks that the editor really shows about 100 pages and fails below 90, so a document that comes out too small can't slip through as \"same\".\n- **Typing:** A types `abcdef` at 5 places spread through the document (10/30/50/70/90%), 30 characters in all. After each character, B waits until it appears in B's model. A separate check confirms all five places actually received the typed text before the model is compared.\n- **Checks:** model, sent (A and B), reopened and converted are compared as for the other cases. For this case, shown is B's screen, hashed after `settle` on every page that was typed on. That covers the stale-pixel risk beyond the first page that the goal names.\n- **Timing:** B's busy time (handler time and long-task time) and typing latency (median and max) are each printed as the median of 3 runs. The 2nd and 3rd runs each use a fresh upload, so typing from earlier runs doesn't carry over.\n- **Existing cases:** the only behavior changes to them are refactors. `play` gains an optional `arg` and `pause`, both defaulting to the old behavior, and upload/open moved into `openPair` unchanged. No assertion was weakened, and `sdkjs-word.sh` now regenerates inputs when `large.docx` is missing.\n\n**Characterize rule:** both surprises in the log are kept in the oracle.\n- The page-count shortfall became the \"at least 90 pages\" guard.\n- The near-zero WebSocket handler time (`recv`) is still printed next to the long-task figure (`long`), and the log explains why `long` is the one to read.\n\nThere is no `.theseus/spawn/` directory and the log asks for no follow-ups, so nothing is missing there. The 